From bdeac6e125ef9288cdb38d887753b8da49147bde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:29:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER (tools 0152): F5's build progress bar always shows
 -- the extension starts on F5; the % in the status bar too
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 1003, a screenshot of F5's terminal "[ 37%] Built target ...": "能做成進度條嗎?"
- Why there was no bar: the extension only started with a designer page / view /
  command (no activationEvents); VS Code reopened at 18:55 and F5 pressed at once
  -> not started (exthost.log: no ht9045 activation), so the build watch never ran.
- package.json "activationEvents": ["onDebug"]: F5 starts it, before the
  preLaunchTask. A build task already running when it starts is taken up
  (tasks.taskExecutions; the time counted from CMake's progress start).
- Not onStartupFinished: tried, the real-VS-Code BtnPanelLane3 selection timed
  out twice in a row (passes without it) -- starting this early slows other things.
- The status bar also shows the build: "建置 ████████░░ 75%（30/40）" (steps /
  CMake's count.txt), seen with the notification folded or Do Not Disturb on;
  hidden when the build ends.

Tests: run_all 3/3 layers (the status bar text, hidden at the end, onDebug);
real VS Code 156/159 (the 3 known stale checks).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
